# Netlify redirects for moderndive.com (this file is served from the gh-pages
# publish root; the main-branch deploy uses clean:false, so it persists).

# Instructor resources hub — built and deployed once to its own Netlify site,
# proxied here so BOTH URLs serve the same content:
#   https://moderndive-instructor-resources.netlify.app  (origin deploy)
#   https://moderndive.com/v2/instructor-resources/      (this proxy; the URL
#                                                         stays on moderndive.com)
#
# Rule 1: the exact hub path (Netlify matches it with OR without the trailing
# slash) 301s to /index.html — WITHOUT this, the bare no-slash form serves the
# hub index at /v2/instructor-resources, and the browser resolves the page's
# relative links against /v2/ (e.g. "syllabus.html" -> /v2/syllabus.html, 404).
# Redirecting to index.html (a DIFFERENT path) avoids the self-loop that a
# plain no-slash -> slash rule causes under Netlify's slash normalization.
# Rule 2: transparent proxy (200) for everything under the hub prefix.
/v2/instructor-resources /v2/instructor-resources/index.html 301!
/v2/instructor-resources/* https://moderndive-instructor-resources.netlify.app/:splat 200

